- # The fallback for a submission launch we can't tie to a student on the roster:
- # a URL Canvas stored before the marker named a student, a member who has since
- # left the course, or a student's marker presented by another student. Resolvable
- # launches get the column's own view narrowed to that student instead
- # (LtiAssignmentViews#submission_focus_user).
- #
- # Canvas's own answer here is "No Preview Available", because an AGS score carries
- # no submitted artifact — this says so in our own words and points at the
- # Dashboard, where the work actually is.
.lti-iframe__landing
  = image_tag '/assets/images/wiki-logo.png', alt: 'Wiki Education Dashboard', class: 'lti-iframe__logo'
  %h1.lti-iframe__title.lti-iframe__title--plain
    = t('lti.assignment_view.submission.explanation')
  - if @submission_course
    = link_to "/courses/#{@submission_course.slug}", target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener',
              class: 'button dark lti-iframe__button' do
      = t('lti.assignment_view.submission.open_dashboard')
      %span.icon.icon-z-external-link_white{ 'aria-hidden': 'true' }
